    {
      "slide": 9,
      "blocks": [
        [
          "Does forecasting accuracy differ across countries?"
        ],
        [
          "Forecasting accuracy varies across the five countries, with no single approach consistently outperforming the benchmarks in every market."
        ],
        [
          "Key finding"
        ],
        [
          "Model performance is country-dependent. Poland’s larger forecasting errors heavily influence pooled results, highlighting the importance of examining accuracy beyond aggregate metrics."
        ],
        [
          "3 of 5",
          "countries had their lowest test RMSE under the macro-only regression: France, Germany and Portugal"
        ],
        [
          "~54%",
          "of the pooled squared error under zero growth came from Poland, despite each country contributing the same number of forecasts"
        ]
      ],
      "notes": [],
